WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:04.340
China’s spies have gotten a lot of unwanted attention recently

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:08.580
thanks in part to political and trade tensions between China and the U.S.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.680
Many of those spies work for the country's main intelligence agency,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.640
the Ministry of State Security - or MSS.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:25.100
In December 2018, one of China’s top tech executives was arrested in Canada on a U.S. extradition request -

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:30.420
soon after, MSS agents abruptly detained two Canadians in China.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:36.100
Then days later the U.S. publicly named two of MSS’s alleged assets

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:41.500
as part of a sweeping U.S. indictment involving hacking on a global scale.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:47.100
The series of events has people asking - what exactly is the MSS?

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.400
This is your Bloomberg QuickTake on China’s elusive spies.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.960
Compared with the U.S., the MSS is something of a mash-up.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.620
It conducts intelligence operations abroad - like the CIA;

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:07.220
counterespionage at home - like the FBI; and cyber-snooping - like the NSA.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:31.680
What is clear, is that the MSS is key to Chinese President Xi Jinping’s efforts to tighten control over security.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:38.260
Its head - Chen Wenqing - is an ex-police chief who helped direct Xi's nationwide anti-graft campaign.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:43.360
In 2015, the National Security Law extended the MSS's power

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:47.220
to outer space and the deep sea as well as the internet.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:07.260
The MSS operates secret detention facilities within China

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.560
and is known for its harsh treatment of dissidents.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:16.580
For example, the blind civil-rights lawyer Chen Guangcheng was under house arrest for 19 months

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:22.380
before he fled to the U.S. Embassy in Beijing in 2012 and eventually moved to New York.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:51.660
Media reports have noted some key MSS victories including the possibility that

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:56.940
they monitored president Donald Trump’s calls made on unsecured cellular devices.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:03.880
There was also a report that the MSS had dismantled CIA operations in China over several years -

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.300
killing a dozen or more of the agency's sources -

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.400
reportedly in one of the worst U.S. intelligence breaches in decades.

